# Test: IS-IS references a LOGICAL interface name decoupled from the kernel
# device via the iface os-name selector (spec-iface-resolve-2 + IS-IS migration).
#
# VALIDATES: a config that names an ethernet interface `uplink` bound to kernel
#            device `eth0` via the os-name selector, and runs IS-IS on the
#            logical name `uplink`, validates through both the iface and isis
#            schemas. This is the config-surface proof of the logical-name
#            decoupling; live resolution to the real kernel device is proven by
#            the QEMU integration tests (iface TestResolveRemapsLogicalNameToOSDevice
#            and isis TestISISAdjacencyUpVeth, both routed through iface.Resolve).
# PREVENTS:  a regression where os-name is not accepted on an ethernet interface
#            (the selector was hidden/dormant before this unit), or IS-IS rejects
#            an interface name that is not itself a kernel device name.
#
# PLATFORM: the `interface { backend netlink }` block is linux-only; skip on
# darwin per rules/os-specific-tests.md.
option=skip-os:value=darwin

# --- Valid: logical name `uplink` -> kernel `eth0`, IS-IS on `uplink`. --------
stdin=isis-logical:terminator=EOF_OK
interface {
	backend netlink
	ethernet uplink {
		os-name eth0
	}
}
isis {
	net 49.0001.0000.0000.0001.00
	level l1-l2
	interfaces {
		interface uplink {
			circuit-type point-to-point
			level l1-l2
		}
	}
}
EOF_OK

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=isis-logical
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid
